00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:51.900
There was a camera on a tripod, and sitting beside the camera was the casting associate, Phyllis,
房间里架着一台三脚架摄像机，摄像机旁边坐着选角助理菲利斯，

253
00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:54.680
my future party planning committee rival.
也就是我未来的“派对策划委员会”竞争对手。

254
00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.580
I was to read with her.
我得和她对戏。

255
00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:01.360
Greg was sitting in the very back of the room, and neither of us made eye contact.
格雷格坐在房间的最深处，我们俩都没有眼神交流。

256
00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:05.060
My agent told me they were having everyone read two scenes,
我的经纪人告诉我，他们让每个人都试读两场戏，

257
00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.920
but if they liked you, they asked you to do a third.
但如果他们看中了你，就会让你再演第三场。

258
00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:11.900
Phyllis and I read my first two scenes, and everyone was laughing.
我和菲利斯演完了前两场戏，大家都笑了。

259
00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.020
It felt great.
感觉棒极了。

260
00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:16.420
Then I was asked to do a third.
然后他们让我演了第三场。

261
00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.960
I worked hard to contain my excitement.
我努力克制住内心的激动。

262
00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.440
Phyllis and I began the final scene,
我和菲利斯开始了最后一场戏的表演，

263
00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:24.920
the one where Michael fake-fires Pam in front of Ryan the Temp.
就是迈克尔在临时工瑞安面前假装解雇帕姆的那一场。

264
00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:29.500
To jog your memory, in the scene, Michael wants to prank Pam
帮你们回忆一下，在那场戏里，迈克尔想捉弄帕姆，

265
00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.860
by pretending to fire her for stealing post-it notes.
假装因为她偷拿便利贴而解雇她。

266
00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:37.380
The fake firing goes terribly wrong, and Pam is very upset.
这场假解雇演砸了，帕姆非常难过。

267
00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.480
She starts to cry and calls Michael a jerk.
她开始哭泣，并骂迈克尔是个混蛋。

268
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.380
The scene was going well.
戏演得很顺利。

269
00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:44.660
Phyllis was killing it as Michael.
菲利斯演迈克尔演得太棒了。

270
00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:47.900
Imagine someone with Phyllis's sweet face
想象一下，一个长着菲利斯那样甜美面孔的人，

271
00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.500
smugly telling you that you've been punked.
一脸得意地告诉你，你被整蛊了。

272
00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.620
When we got to the part where I was supposed to tear up
当我们演到我应该泪流满面，

273
00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:54.880
and call Michael a jerk,
并骂迈克尔是混蛋的那部分时，

274
00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:58.280
I really let Michael slash Phyllis have it.
我真的对“迈克尔版菲利斯”发火了。

275
00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:02.800
Now, there are three times you can tell I am from Texas.
其实，有三种情况能听出我是德州人。

276
00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.520
When I am tired, tipsy, or pissed off.
当我累了、喝醉了，或者生气的时候。

277
00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:10.460
So I definitely slipped into a southern drawl as I growled,
所以我咆哮时，绝对带上了南方口音，

278
00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:11.220
Jerk!
“混蛋！”

279
00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:15.900
The room of producers burst out laughing, and I remember thinking,
满屋子的制片人哄堂大笑，我记得当时心想，

280
00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:20.940
Hmm, not so sure I'm supposed to get a laugh at this point, but okay.
嗯，我不确定这儿是不是该有笑点，但好吧。

281
00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:22.640
And that was it.
就这样结束了。

282
00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.620
Allison thanked me for coming in.
艾莉森感谢我过来试镜。

283
00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:28.300
Greg discreetly smiled from the back row and gave me a thumbs up,
格雷格在后排低调地笑了笑，对我竖起了大拇指，

284
00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.780
and I walked out of there on cloud nine.
我走出房间时简直高兴得要飞起来了。

285
00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.900
I just knew I had that part.
我当时就觉得这角色非我莫属。

286
00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.840
The next day, I got a call from Allison.
第二天，我接到了艾莉森的电话。

287
00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:37.700
I did not get that part.
我没拿到那个角色。

288
00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:42.020
She told me they really liked me but thought I was a little too feisty for Pam.
她说他们真的很喜欢我，但觉得我演帕姆的话有点太泼辣了。

289
00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.980
I was disappointed, of course, but I felt good about my audition,
我当然很失望，但我对自己的试镜表现感觉良好，

290
00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.700
and I was thankful for the opportunity.
我也很感激这次机会。

291
00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:51.000
So I let it go, and I moved on.
所以我放下了这件事，继续前行。

292
00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.280
That's just what you have to do as an actor.
作为演员，你只能这么做。

293
00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:58.400
Plus, I had another audition that week for an improv pilot that I was really excited about.
况且，那周我还有一个即兴表演试播集的试镜，我对此非常兴奋。

294
00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:03.440
It was about a group of people working at a hair salon in New York City for the Oxygen Network.
那是为Oxygen电视网制作的，关于一群在纽约美发沙龙工作的人的故事。

295
00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.720
The working title was Salon Royale.
暂定名是《皇家沙龙》。

296
00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.580
I auditioned for the role of the promiscuous receptioniSt.
我试镜的角色是那个滥情的接待员。

297
00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:12.600
Feisty was no problem here.
在这里，“泼辣”完全不是问题。

298
00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.760
And I was caSt.
我被选中了。

299
00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:19.400
The producers of that show flew me out to New York City first class.
那部剧的制片人让我头等舱飞往纽约。

300
00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:19.500
class.
舱位。

301
00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:23.760
I had never flown first class for work, and it felt so fancy.
我以前从未因公坐过头等舱，感觉真是太高级了。

302
00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:26.220
The cast was full of amazing
演员阵容里全是了不起的

303
00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:31.160
improvisers—Ian Roberts, Beth Cahill, Dave Rozowski—and the show was written and directed
即兴表演者——伊恩·罗伯茨、贝丝·卡希尔、戴夫·罗佐夫斯基——而节目是由

304
00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:32.200
by Emmy Laybourne.
艾美·莱伯恩编剧和导演的。

305
00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:37.180
Emmy's mom, Geraldine, was the president of Oxygen at the time, so I thought
艾美的母亲杰拉尔丁当时是Oxygen频道的总裁，所以我以为

306
00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.000
we had a good shot of making it to series.
我们很有机会拍成系列剧。

307
00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:43.460
But alas, we didn't get picked up, so back to Los
但遗憾的是，我们没被选中，所以我又回到了

308
00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:44.500
Angeles, I went.
洛杉矶。

309
00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:49.580
After back-to-back rejections, I was feeling pretty discouraged about acting.
接连遭遇拒绝后，我对演戏感到相当沮丧。

310
00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:54.520
I decided to concentrate my energy on writing and put acting on hold for a while.
我决定把精力集中在写作上，暂时搁置演艺事业。

311
00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:59.220
Several weeks went by, and I was feeling good about my decision to lean into writing.
几周过去了，我对专注于写作的决定感觉良好。

312
00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.940
And then I got a call that changed everything.
然后我接到了一通改变一切的电话。

313
00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.880
I was working the box office at iOS when I got
当时我正在iOS售票处工作，接到了

314
00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:07.940
a call on my flip phone.
翻盖手机打来的电话。

315
00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:08.920
Remember those?
还记得那种手机吗？

316
00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.980
It was a number I didn't recognize, so I let it go to
那是一个我不认识的号码，所以我让它转到了

317
00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:12.540
voicemail.
语音信箱。

318
00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.920
As it turns out, it was from Allison Jones's office.
结果发现，那是艾莉森·琼斯办公室打来的。

319
00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.180
The producers of the office wanted
《办公室》的制片人想

320
00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:21.980
to see me again for a new role, the prickly lady in accounting.
再见我一次，为了一个新角色，会计部那个刻薄的女士。

321
00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.520
Allison told me the creative team
艾莉森告诉我，创意团队

322
00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:28.380
thought I was right for the world of Dunder Mifflin, just not quite right for Pam.
认为我适合邓德·米夫林的世界，只是不太适合演帕姆。

323
00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:29.900
This time,
这一次，

324
00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.380
there was no big room full of producers.
没有坐满制片人的大房间。

325
00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:34.080
It was just the director, Ken Kwapis, Phyllis, and the
只有导演肯·卡皮斯、菲利斯，还有

326
00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:34.420
tripod.
三脚架。

327
00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:39.780
I was told to come in wearing something drab, my hair plain, and with little to no makeup.
我被告知要穿得朴素点，头发梳得简单些，几乎不化妆或完全不化妆。

328
00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:43.660
Apparently, the prickly lady in accounting was no fashion plate.
显然，会计部那个刻薄的女士可不是什么时尚达人。

329
00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:48.220
I wore a light blue turtleneck sweater with a gray cardigan and black pants,
我穿了一件浅蓝色高领毛衣，外面套着灰色开衫，下身穿黑色长裤，

330
00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:51.780
pulled my hair back in a low ponytail, and left my face bare.
把头发扎成低马尾，素面朝天。

331
00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.760
I channeled all my sass, and I got the part.
我拿出了我所有的傲气，最终拿下了这个角色。

332
00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:01.660
And I was pretty sure that the prickly accountant would be an easier role for my mom to talk about
而且我非常确定，对于我妈妈来说，在她的女士圣经研习会上谈论这个刻薄的会计，

333
00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:05.900
at her lady's Bible study than the lustful salon receptioniSt.
要比谈论那个风骚的沙龙接待员容易得多。

334
00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.600
So everything worked out.
所以一切都圆满解决了。

335
00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:12.440
I am so grateful to Greg for getting me in that room on November 17th.
我非常感谢格雷格让我能在11月17日走进那个房间。

336
00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:14.700
That moment changed my life forever.
那一刻永远改变了我的生活。

337
00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:21.820
And little did I know, the gal that was cast in the role of Pam would become my best friend forever.
我当时根本没想到，那个被选为帕姆的女孩会成为我一生的挚友。

338
00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:29.240
Before we started taping the first episode, Ken Kwapis suggested we all personalize our desks.
在开始拍摄第一集之前，肯·卡皮斯建议我们每个人都个性化布置一下自己的办公桌。

339
00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.020
I loved this idea.
我喜欢这个主意。

340
00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.020
Because of my real-life office experience,
因为我有过现实中的办公室经验，

341
00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:38.820
I had very strong feelings about the types of supplies a receptionist should have on their
对于接待员的桌子上应该放些什么办公用品，

342
00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:39.200
desk.
我有非常强烈的想法。

343
00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:43.300
The invitation to personalize my workspace made me very excited.
布置自己工作空间的邀请让我感到非常兴奋。

344
00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.180
Ken also suggested John
肯还建议约翰·卡拉辛斯基

345
00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:49.880
Krasinski and I spend some time getting to know each other outside of work.
和我花点时间在工作之外多了解彼此。

346
00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:51.420
Have lunch.
一起吃午饭。

347
00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:52.220
Have
喝

348
00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:52.760
coffee.
咖啡。

349
00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:57.500
Create a rapport, was the suggestion, as it will translate on screen.
建议是建立一种默契，因为这会体现在银幕上。

350
00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:59.420
This is common for
这在业内很常见

351
00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:01.540
actors who are cast in a new project together.
共同出演新项目的演员们。

352
00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:04.420
It's key to try and get to know the people you're
试着去了解那些你即将

353
00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:08.780
going to be pretending to be in a relationship with so you don't seem like total strangers on
假装在谈恋爱的人是非常关键的，这样你们在

354
00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:09.160
screen.
银幕上才不会显得像完全的陌生人。

355
00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:15.900
For example, during rehearsals for my job on ABC's Splitting Up Together, Oliver Hudson and
例如，在为ABC电视台的《分分合合》工作排练期间，奥利弗·哈德森和

356
00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:20.080
I spent two days hanging out with the three children who would play our kids on the show.
我花了整整两天时间，和剧中饰演我们孩子的三个小演员待在一起。

357
00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:25.360
Like real parents, we sat reading each other bits of news articles off our phones while the kids
就像真正的父母一样，我们坐在一起，互相读着手机上的新闻片段，而孩子们

358
00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:25.840
wrestled.
则在一旁打闹。

359
00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:30.980
When I did the movie Hall Pass, I had drinks with Owen Wilson, who was playing my husband.
当我拍电影《放风通行证》时，我和饰演我丈夫的欧文·威尔逊一起喝了酒。

360
00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:37.840
Incidentally, I did not meet up with Scott Wolfe before rubbing Charlie, and, well, you already know
顺便提一下，在拍摄《查理》之前我并没有和斯科特·沃尔夫见面，嗯，你们已经知道

361
00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:38.600
how that worked out.
结果如何了。

362
00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:43.220
Note, Scott Wolfe is a delightful human being, and I adore him.
注意，斯科特·沃尔夫是个可爱的人，我很喜欢他。

363
00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:43.540
It is
这

364
00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:45.300
not our fault the show didn't go.
不是我们的错，剧集没能继续下去。

365
00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:46.500
We were fantastic.
我们表现得非常出色。

366
00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:50.080
And I couldn't forget what Stephen Merchant had
而且我无法忘记斯蒂芬·莫昌特所

367
00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:55.540
said, that John and I, virtual strangers, were to be the heart of the show.
说的话，他说我和约翰，这两个几乎陌生的人，将成为这部剧的核心。

368
00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:57.820
So one night after
所以有一天排练后，

369
00:21:57.820 --> 00:22:00.900
rehearsals, we decided to kill two birds with one stone.
我们决定一箭双雕。

370
00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:03.560
John Krasinski and I went to a nearby
约翰·卡拉辛斯基和我去了附近的一家

371
00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:07.220
office supply store and shopped for things to decorate our desks.
办公用品店，挑选装饰我们办公桌的东西。

372
00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:10.100
I got a label maker, message
我买了一台标签机、留言

373
00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:14.360
pad, message sorter, daily calendar, file folders, multicolored sticky notes.
便签纸、文件整理架、日历、文件夹、彩色便利贴。

374
00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:15.760
The list goes on and on.
清单列都列不完。

375
00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:19.200
I left with two bags of supplies.
我提着两大袋办公用品离开了。

376
00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:23.120
I think John got a tape dispenser and maybe some post-it notes.
我想约翰只买了一个胶带座，可能还有一些便利贴。

377
00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:28.620
The whole time we were shopping, we just kept talking about how excited we were to start
整个购物过程中，我们一直在谈论对即将开始

378
00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:29.020
shooting.
拍摄的兴奋之情。

379
00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:32.880
We wanted to do everything we could to go from pilot to series.
我们想尽一切努力让试播集变成正式剧集。

380
00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:38.100
John also shared about moving from New York and the adjustment to living in Los Angeles.
约翰还分享了他从纽约搬来，以及适应洛杉矶生活的过程。

381
00:22:38.600 --> 00:22:43.020
I was happy to learn that we were both pretty boring people, in a good way.
很高兴得知我们都是相当无趣的人，当然，这是褒义的。

382
00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:44.960
He felt stable.
他给人的感觉很稳重。

383
00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:48.420
He had a good work ethic, and he was funny.
他有很好的职业道德，而且很幽默。

384
00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:49.940
We laughed a lot.
我们笑得很开心。

385
00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:54.040
I could tell he was going to be a good acting partner.
我看得出来他会是一个很好的表演搭档。

386
00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:59.900
Greg had encouraged us to think about our characters and their backstories,
格雷格鼓励我们思考自己的角色及其背景故事，

387
00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:01.720
so when it came to my desk area,
所以当谈到我的办公桌区域时，

388
00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:05.740
I tried to imagine what a stuffy lady in accounting might bring to the office.
我试着想象一位古板的会计女士会带什么东西到办公室。

389
00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:08.900
I brought in a photo of my grandmother, Lena, and me.
我带了一张我和祖母莉娜的合影。

390
00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.820
In the picture, my eyes are closed, but I am smiling.
照片里我闭着眼睛，但我正在微笑。

391
00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:16.600
It makes me laugh that Angela Martin would choose to frame a photo where her eyes are closed.
安吉拉·马丁竟然会选择装裱一张自己闭着眼睛的照片，这让我觉得很好笑。

392
00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:19.760
Like, perhaps that was just the best one of the bunch?
就像是，也许那已经是那一堆照片里最好的一张了？

393
00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:22.020
I also brought in a day planner.
我还带了一个日程规划本。

394
00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:26.400
I felt like Angela Martin would have an appointment book and it would be very comprehensive.
我觉得安吉拉·马丁会有一个非常详尽的预约簿。

395
00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:31.240
The set dressers put a blue ceramic cat paperclip holder on my desk.
布景师在我的桌上放了一个蓝色陶瓷猫形回形针座。

396
00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:35.960
The cat's left ear was slightly chipped, and I loved that little detail.
猫的左耳有一点缺口，我很喜欢这个小细节。

397
00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:40.520
It looked like a knick-knack you would get from a garage sale in a small town.
它看起来就像那种你在小镇旧货摊上买到的小摆件。

398
00:23:41.240 --> 00:23:45.320
That cat paperclip holder did a lot to inform who Angela Martin was.
那个猫形回形针座对塑造安吉拉·马丁这个角色起到了很大的作用。

399
00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.260
It was clear to me that she must love cats
我很清楚她一定很爱猫，

400
00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:51.400
and that she didn't need fancy new things to make her happy.
而且她不需要昂贵的新东西就能感到快乐。

401
00:23:51.720 --> 00:23:56.040
She was too humble for fancy, in a judgmental way, of course.
她为人太谦逊，以至于显得有些虚伪，当然，这是带着批判眼光的看法。

402
00:23:56.940 --> 00:24:00.580
People ask us all the time what we took from the set the day we wrapped the series,
人们总是问我们，在剧集杀青那天我们从片场带走了什么，

403
00:24:01.060 --> 00:24:03.040
and I took that cat paperclip holder.
我带走了那个猫咪造型的曲别针座。

404
00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:05.740
It sits on my desk at home to this day.
直到今天，它还放在我家的书桌上。

405
00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:11.640
Walking onto the set for our first day of shooting, I was so nervous.
拍摄第一天走进片场时，我非常紧张。

406
00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.400
I'd left my house at 5 a.m.
我早上五点就离开了家，

407
00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:16.440
for what was a 45-minute commute.
那段路程通常需要四十五分钟。

408
00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:21.640
I made myself a song mix I affectionately titled Songs of Scranton.
我给自己做了一份混音带，亲切地命名为《斯克兰顿之歌》。

409
00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:24.920
I drank coffee and bounced along the freeway.
我喝着咖啡，在高速公路上随着音乐晃动。

410
00:24:25.140 --> 00:24:30.820
I tried to imagine I was driving to my real job at a real paper company in Scranton, Pennsylvania.
我试着想象自己正开车去宾夕法尼亚州斯克兰顿的一家真正的造纸公司上班。

411
00:24:31.640 --> 00:24:33.880
When I arrived, I was taken to wardrobe.
到达后，我被带去了服装组。

412
00:24:34.420 --> 00:24:40.780
There were a lot of very quick introductions to various other cast members who were coming and going between wardrobe, hair, and makeup.
当时有许多匆忙的介绍，各种演员在服装、发型和化妆间之间来来往往。

413
00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:48.140
It was then that I first met Leslie David Baker, who would soon be known to many as Stanley Hudson.
就在那时，我第一次见到了莱斯利·大卫·贝克，他后来被许多人熟知为斯坦利·哈德森。

414
00:24:48.740 --> 00:24:56.360
He was so warm, friendly, and open that watching him switch over to Stanley, the checked-out grump, was hilarious.
他本人非常热情、友好且开朗，看着他切换成斯坦利那个心不在焉的怪老头形象，真是太搞笑了。

415
00:24:57.200 --> 00:25:03.020
Our director had requested that everyone be on set and at our desks at 7.30 a.m.
我们的导演要求所有人早上七点半准时到达片场，

416
00:25:03.180 --> 00:25:03.360
sharp.
坐在各自的工位上。

417
00:25:03.780 --> 00:25:07.540
He asked us all to pretend to work while the film crew recorded us.
他让我们假装工作，同时让摄制组记录下我们。

418
00:25:08.160 --> 00:25:11.380
He wanted to capture us like real documentarians would,
他想像真正的纪录片制作人那样捕捉我们的状态，

419
00:25:11.560 --> 00:25:13.820
because this was the convention of the show.
因为这就是这部剧的拍摄准则。

420
00:25:14.040 --> 00:25:18.080
We were real office workers being filmed by a documentary film crew.
我们是真正的办公室职员，被一个纪录片摄制组拍摄着。

421
00:25:18.560 --> 00:25:22.340
When we were all in place, the set was cleared of all crew members
当我们各就各位后，片场清空了所有工作人员，

422
00:25:22.340 --> 00:25:25.740
except for the camera operator, boom operator, and director.
只留下了摄影师、收音师和导演。

423
00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:30.960
They started rolling, and it all felt so real.
他们开始拍摄，一切感觉都太真实了。

424
00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:33.820
It was very quiet at firSt.
起初非常安静。

425
00:25:34.570 --> 00:25:38.200
Then Phyllis and Leslie started improvising fake sales calls.
然后菲利斯和莱斯利开始即兴表演虚假的销售电话。

426
00:25:38.780 --> 00:25:41.680
I started to answer the phone and transfer calls.
我开始接听电话并转接通话。

427
00:25:41.980 --> 00:25:47.140
A lot of the shots you see in the opening credits of the show are from that very first morning.
你在片头字幕中看到的许多镜头，都是那天清晨拍摄的。

428
00:25:48.840 --> 00:25:51.480
I was also a bundle of nerves that first day.
第一天我也紧张得不行。

429
00:25:51.820 --> 00:25:56.300
My call time to set was 4.30 a.m., so I didn't get much sleep the night before.
我被要求凌晨四点半到达片场，所以前一天晚上我没怎么睡。

430
00:25:56.680 --> 00:26:00.420
We were filming in an empty office building in Culver City, California.
我们在加州卡尔弗城的一栋空办公楼里拍摄。

431
00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:04.000
The building was only two stories, and we filmed on the second floor.
那栋楼只有两层，我们在二楼拍摄。

432
00:26:04.680 --> 00:26:09.020
There was an empty soundstage next to the main building where the hair and makeup team was set up.
主楼旁边有一个空的摄影棚，发型和化妆团队就设在那里。

433
00:26:09.380 --> 00:26:14.640
It was cold and dark when I arrived, with only one small space heater in that big drafty room.
我到达时又冷又黑，那个巨大的通风房间里只有一个小取暖器。

434
00:26:14.980 --> 00:26:17.200
We huddled around it and waited our turn.
我们围在它周围，等待轮到自己。

435
00:26:17.740 --> 00:26:22.180
Our director had instructed the hair and makeup departments to keep our looks very simple.
导演指示发型和化妆部门让我们的造型保持非常朴素。

436
00:26:22.720 --> 00:26:26.000
I was given a loose French braid and some powder and lip balm.
我被梳了一个松散的法式辫子，只涂了一点粉底和润唇膏。

437
00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:27.080
That's all.
仅此而已。

438
00:26:27.540 --> 00:26:32.380
The wardrobe department asked me to bring the clothes and shoes I had worn to my audition for Angela Martin,
服装部门让我带上我面试安吉拉·马丁这个角色时穿的衣服和鞋子，

439
00:26:32.380 --> 00:26:35.080
so I actually wore my own clothes in the pilot.
所以我实际上在试播集中穿的是我自己的衣服。

440
00:26:35.780 --> 00:26:38.140
With barely any hair and makeup and no wardrobe
几乎不需要什么发型和化妆，也没有服装

441
00:26:38.140 --> 00:26:40.380
fitting, it didn't take much time for me to get ready.
试穿，我很快就准备好了。

442
00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:43.560
I walked onto the set early and realized
我早早走进片场，意识到

443
00:26:43.560 --> 00:26:46.360
I wasn't sure where I was supposed to sit.
我不确定自己该坐在哪里。

444
00:26:47.160 --> 00:26:49.540
Ken Quapis must have seen me looking around sort of
肯·夸皮斯一定看到了我那副

445
00:26:49.540 --> 00:26:54.240
loSt. He came over to me and told me I'd be sitting in the corner in what would become the
迷茫的样子。他走过来告诉我，我将坐在角落里，也就是后来成为

446
00:26:54.240 --> 00:26:55.100
accounting department.
会计部门的地方。

447
00:26:55.680 --> 00:26:58.260
He walked me over to introduce me to my deskmates.
他带我过去，把我介绍给我的邻座。

448
00:26:58.900 --> 00:26:59.780
There I found
在那里我发现

449
00:26:59.780 --> 00:27:03.800
seated at the desk right next to me, Oscar Nunez.
坐在我旁边桌子上的，是奥斯卡·努内兹。

450
00:27:04.200 --> 00:27:06.580
I had known Oscar for years.
我认识奥斯卡很多年了。

451
00:27:07.120 --> 00:27:08.380
We first met at the
我们第一次见面是在

452
00:27:08.380 --> 00:27:13.120
Groundlings and then went on to perform together in a sketch comedy show called Hot Towel.
Groundlings剧团，后来又一起出演了一个叫《热毛巾》的素描喜剧节目。

453
00:27:13.420 --> 00:27:14.160
I played
我扮演的是

454
00:27:14.160 --> 00:27:16.560
a horny boy scout and Oscar a crazy professor.
一个好色的童子军，奥斯卡扮演一个疯狂的教授。

455
00:27:17.360 --> 00:27:20.060
I was so thrilled to see my old friend that I yelled
见到老朋友我太激动了，以至于大喊

456
00:27:20.060 --> 00:27:22.120
out, holy crap, Oscar.
出来，天哪，奥斯卡。

457
00:27:22.980 --> 00:27:27.480
Neither of us knew that the other had been caSt. This was in the antiquated
我们俩都不知道对方也被选中了。那是在那个古老的

458
00:27:27.480 --> 00:27:30.720
times before everything everyone is doing and saying was posted online.
时代，在每个人所做所说的一切都被发布到网上之前。

459
00:27:30.980 --> 00:27:32.260
You could still be
你仍然可以

460
00:27:32.260 --> 00:27:33.440
surprised by things.
对事物感到惊喜。

461
00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:34.800
Imagine that.
想象一下。

462
00:27:35.800 --> 00:27:39.480
One of the very first photos I took on The Office set was of the
我在《办公室》片场拍的第一张照片之一是

463
00:27:39.480 --> 00:27:40.340
accounting department.
会计部门的。

464
00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:43.960
We took the photo in character, and it cracks me up that even in the
我们是按角色拍的那张照片，让我觉得好笑的是，即使在

465
00:27:43.960 --> 00:27:47.800
first week, Oscar, Kevin, and Angela were clearly formed people.
第一周，奥斯卡、凯文和安吉拉就已经是非常鲜活的人物了。

466
00:27:48.260 --> 00:27:50.200
We already knew who we were in the
我们已经知道自己在

467
00:27:50.200 --> 00:27:50.960
world of the show.
剧中的定位了。

468
00:27:51.220 --> 00:27:55.380
I think it speaks to how amazing the writing was on The Office, and also
我认为这说明了《办公室》的剧本有多棒，也说明了

469
00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:59.360
to Allison Jones and her gift for assembling acting ensembles.
艾莉森·琼斯在组建演员阵容方面的天赋。

470
00:28:01.170 --> 00:28:06.430
I'll never forget seeing Angela pop her head up over the partition between our desks to introduce
我永远不会忘记看到安吉拉从我们办公桌之间的隔板上探出头来介绍

471
00:28:06.430 --> 00:28:06.890
herself.
她自己。

472
00:28:07.270 --> 00:28:12.910
Her face barely made it over the edge as she said, hello, in her bubbly Texas twang.
她那张脸勉强从边缘露出来，用她那活泼的德州口音说了声“你好”。

473
00:28:13.310 --> 00:28:16.630
She was instantly funny, upbeat, and kind.
她立刻就显得风趣、乐观又善良。

474
00:28:16.890 --> 00:28:18.350
I liked her immediately.
我立刻就喜欢上了她。

475
00:28:19.010 --> 00:28:21.110
She was clearly nothing like her
她显然和她的

476
00:28:21.110 --> 00:28:24.430
character Angela Martin, which shows what a great actress she is.
角色安吉拉·马丁一点也不像，这说明她是一位多么出色的演员。

477
00:28:24.890 --> 00:28:26.510
In addition to our chats
除了我们在

478
00:28:26.510 --> 00:28:31.370
over the partition, Angela would talk my ear off in the hair and makeup room, and she would keep
隔板上的聊天，安吉拉还在化妆间里跟我说个不停，而且她会一直

479
00:28:31.370 --> 00:28:34.010
talking as we walked to the snack table and then to set.
说到我们走到零食桌前，然后再走到片场。

480
00:28:34.490 --> 00:28:37.030
I often joke that I had no choice but to
我经常开玩笑说，我别无选择，只能

481
00:28:37.030 --> 00:28:40.250
become friends with Angela because she wouldn't stop talking to me.
和安吉拉成为朋友，因为她不停地跟我说话。

482
00:28:40.730 --> 00:28:42.350
I was so grateful for her.
我非常感激她。

483
00:28:42.930 --> 00:28:45.770
I was nervous, and she was an instant comfort.
我很紧张，而她给了我即时的安慰。

484
00:28:47.720 --> 00:28:50.160
My first memory of Jenna is hearing a little
我对珍娜的第一印象是听到一声小小的

485
00:28:50.160 --> 00:28:53.260
dainty sneeze come from behind the partition next to my desk.
娇气的喷嚏声从我办公桌旁边的隔板后面传来。

486
00:28:53.620 --> 00:28:55.360
It reminded me of my neighbor's
这让我想起了我邻居的

487
00:28:55.360 --> 00:28:56.380
peek-a-poo sneezing.
北京犬和贵宾犬混种狗打喷嚏的样子。

488
00:28:56.660 --> 00:28:58.200
It was adorable.
太可爱了。

489
00:28:58.980 --> 00:29:02.060
She sat directly behind me and was physically the closest
她就坐在我正后方，在片场是离我身体距离

490
00:29:02.060 --> 00:29:03.240
gal to me on set.
最近的姑娘。

491
00:29:04.080 --> 00:29:08.000
Jenna seemed shy, but then again, I am super chatty, and I probably scared her.
珍娜看起来很害羞，但话说回来，我超级健谈，可能把她吓到了。

492
00:29:08.140 --> 00:29:09.440
I can do that to people.
我确实会那样对待别人。

493
00:29:10.080 --> 00:29:13.840
Every day that first week, I'd get up on my tippy-toes and pop my head over
第一周的每一天，我都会踮起脚尖，探出头去

494
00:29:13.840 --> 00:29:14.400
and chat.
和她聊天。

495
00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:19.420
Those desk partition chats became our daily habit for the next nine years.
那些隔板间的聊天成了我们接下来九年的日常习惯。

496
00:29:21.360 --> 00:29:24.060
The whole week seemed to speed by so faSt.
整个星期似乎过得飞快。

497
00:29:24.680 --> 00:29:31.980
Before we knew it, the pilot was done, and we all went home to wait the almost three months it took to learn if our show would make it to series.
还没等我们反应过来，试播集就拍完了，我们都回家等待了近三个月，才得知我们的剧是否能被预订成系列剧。

498
00:29:33.180 --> 00:29:37.120
Shortly after we'd filmed the pilot, I went to London for a friend's wedding.
拍完试播集后不久，我去伦敦参加了一个朋友的婚礼。

499
00:29:37.760 --> 00:29:42.020
While I was there, I reached out to Ricky and Steven to see if they were able to meet.
在那里的时候，我联系了瑞奇和史蒂文，看看他们是否有空见面。

500
00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:48.420
I don't know where I got the courage to call, but since I'd basically been unemployed since shooting the pilot for the office,
我不知道我从哪来的勇气打电话，但自从拍完《办公室》试播集后，我基本上就失业了，

501
00:29:48.420 --> 00:29:51.820
this was the one potentially exciting thing I had in my life.
这是我生活中唯一一件可能令人兴奋的事情。

502
00:29:52.180 --> 00:29:54.260
I wanted to milk it for all it was worth.
我想把它榨干，发挥出它所有的价值。

503
00:29:55.100 --> 00:29:59.140
They agreed to host me for lunch at the exclusive Groucho Club.
他们同意在独家的高尔乔俱乐部请我吃午饭。

504
00:29:59.600 --> 00:30:03.160
The Groucho is a famed private club for comedians,
高尔乔俱乐部是一家著名的喜剧演员私人俱乐部，

505
00:30:03.160 --> 00:30:05.160
and I couldn't believe I was there.
我简直不敢相信自己竟然身处其中。

506
00:30:05.780 --> 00:30:08.020
I don't like to think too much about that lunch
我不愿过多回想那顿午餐，

507
00:30:08.020 --> 00:30:10.300
because I'm certain I sounded like a raving idiot,
因为我肯定自己当时听起来像个胡言乱语的白痴，

508
00:30:10.640 --> 00:30:13.640
going on and on and praising their genius nonstop.
喋喋不休地不停赞美他们的天才。

509
00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:15.960
They must have taken pity on me
他们一定是同情我，

510
00:30:15.960 --> 00:30:18.480
because they even agreed to pose for a photo afterward.
因为他们甚至同意在餐后和我合影。

511
00:30:19.520 --> 00:30:23.980
After the lunch, I was sitting on the tube reading a discarded UK TV guide.
午餐后，我坐在地铁上，读着一份别人丢弃的英国电视指南。

512
00:30:24.460 --> 00:30:29.760
Inside was an article about the casting of the American version of The Office.
里面有一篇关于美版《办公室》选角的文章。

513
00:30:30.200 --> 00:30:32.280
How crazy is that?
这有多疯狂？

514
00:30:32.880 --> 00:30:34.860
The article was not positive.
文章的基调并不正面。

515
00:30:35.280 --> 00:30:36.580
It said, quote,
它写道，引用：

516
00:30:37.040 --> 00:30:40.940
The chances of NBC actually matching wits with the original
NBC能与原版相媲美的几率，

517
00:30:40.940 --> 00:30:44.960
are about as good as finding a designated driver at a Wembley football match.
大概就和在温布利球赛现场找到一个指定代驾一样大。

518
00:30:45.140 --> 00:30:45.740
End quote.
引用结束。

519
00:30:46.420 --> 00:30:52.600
It included photos of the original cast members alongside photos of each of us from the American version.
文章里放了原版演员的照片，旁边还配上了我们美版每个人的照片。

520
00:30:53.200 --> 00:30:58.420
The article basically went on to break down how we were ill-suited for the roles and would ruin the show.
文章基本上一直在分析我们如何不适合这些角色，以及会如何毁掉这部剧。

521
00:30:58.860 --> 00:31:05.580
